            <ArticleTitle>Totally extraperitoneal laparoscopic hernia repair.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>217-23</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Totally extraperitoneal laparoscopic hernia repair is the endoscopic equivalent of the open preperitoneal prosthetic approach. Results from a randomized trial confirm that it is less painful, associated with a more rapid return to normal activity, and associated with an insignificant increase in recurrence rates when compared with open tension-free hernia repair.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
